# Adventurer Bot Improvements

Make bots feel more alive by adding inter-city walking routes, idle micro-behaviors, and time-of-day awareness, all within [Adventurer.kt](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/content/global/bots/Adventurer.kt).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **GE behavior question**: Currently bots only visit the GE when their `city` is set to one of the 4 GE clerk/banker locations. If a bot walks to `varrock` (the regular city point), it does **not** naturally walk to the GE. This plan adds a chance for bots in Varrock to walk over to the GE, is that what you want?

> [!WARNING]
> **Teleporting still exists as a fallback.** Routes won't cover every city pair, so bots will still teleport when no defined route exists. The goal here is to **reduce** teleporting, not eliminate it entirely.

## Proposed Changes

All changes are to a single file:

### Adventurer Bot Core

#### [MODIFY] [Adventurer.kt](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/content/global/bots/Adventurer.kt)

---

**Feature 1: Waypoint Routes + `State.WALKING_PATH`**

Add a `routes` map in the companion object defining walking paths between nearby cities. Each route is an `Array<Location>` of waypoints that [walkArray](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/core/game/bots/ScriptAPI.kt#360-387) can follow.

```kotlin
// Example routes (will define ~8-10 key routes covering both city groups)
val routes = mapOf(
    Pair(varrock, lumbridge) to arrayOf(
        Location(3233, 3395, 0), Location(3233, 3350, 0), 
        Location(3233, 3300, 0), lumbridge
    ),
    Pair(falador, draynor) to arrayOf(
        Location(2965, 3340, 0), Location(2990, 3280, 0), draynor
    ),
    Pair(varrock, edgeville) to arrayOf(
        Location(3175, 3450, 0), Location(3130, 3475, 0), edgeville
    ),
    // ... more routes
)
```

Add new `State.WALKING_PATH` enum value. In the `ADVENTURE` state, when the bot decides to change cities, it will first check for a defined route. If one exists, it uses [walkArray](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/core/game/bots/ScriptAPI.kt#360-387) instead of teleporting. The walking state watches for arrival (within ~5 tiles of destination) and transitions to `ADVENTURE`.

Add a `findRoute(from, to)` helper that checks `routes` for a matching pair in either direction (reversing the waypoint array if needed).

---

**Feature 2: Idle Micro-Behaviors**

Add a new `performIdleBehavior()` function that randomly picks from:

| Behavior | How | When |
|---|---|---|
| **Emote** | `Emotes.WAVE.play(bot)` / `THINK` / `DANCE` / `CHEER` | Near other players, ~15% chance |
| **Examine scenery** | `bot.faceLocation(nearbyScenery.location)` + pause 3-5 ticks | While roaming, ~20% chance |
| **Watch combat** | `bot.faceLocation(fightingEntity.location)` + idle 5-10 ticks | When nearby entity is in combat, ~30% chance |
| **Random chat** | Existing [dialogue()](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/content/global/bots/Adventurer.kt#527-574) function | Near players, ~10% chance |

This function gets called from `ADVENTURE` and `IDLE_GE` states as an alternative to pure standing/walking.

Emotes used will be the simple unlocked ones: `YES`, `NO`, `BOW`, `THINK`, `WAVE`, `SHRUG`, `CHEER`, `LAUGH`, `DANCE`, `CRY`, `CLAP`, `JUMP_FOR_JOY`.

---

**Feature 3: Time-of-Day Awareness**

Add an `isNightTime()` function checking `LocalDateTime.now().hour`:
- **Night** = 10 PM – 6 AM (hours 22, 23, 0-5)
- **Day** = everything else

During night hours:
- Bots roam with **smaller** distances (60% of normal)
- Bots are **less likely** to initiate combat ([immerse()](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/content/global/bots/Adventurer.kt#157-184) combat chance halved)
- Bots are **more likely** to idle at the GE or sit near banks
- Bots **prefer** to stay in their current city rather than traveling

---

**Feature 4: Varrock → GE Natural Walking**

In `State.ADVENTURE`, when `city == varrock`:
- Add a ~15% per-tick chance to walk toward the GE instead of random roaming
- Bot walks to one of the GE social locations using [walkTo](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/core/game/bots/ScriptAPI.kt#349-359)
- Once near the GE, set `city` to a random GE location and transition to normal GE behavior

---

**New State Enum:**

```diff
 enum class State {
     START,
     ADVENTURE,
+    WALKING_PATH,
     FIND_BANK,
     FIND_CITY,
     IDLE_GE,
     GE,
     TELEPORTING,
     LOOT,
     LOOT_DELAY,
     FIND_GE
 }
```

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- No automated unit tests exist for [Adventurer.kt](file:///c:/Users/diya0/IdeaProjects/2009scape/Server/src/main/content/global/bots/Adventurer.kt) in this project, and the bot behavior is inherently visual/observational. Compile check only:
  ```
  cd c:\Users\diya0\IdeaProjects\2009scape\Server
  mvn compile -pl .
  ```

### Manual Verification
Since bot behavior is observational, the best verification is in-game testing. After compiling:

1. **Start the server** and log in with a test account
2. **Spawn several adventurer bots** using the existing bot spawn commands
3. **Observe** the following over ~5-10 minutes:
   - Bots walk between cities instead of always teleporting
   - Bots perform emotes near you (wave, think, dance, etc.)
   - Bots face nearby scenery and pause briefly
   - Bots in Varrock sometimes walk toward the GE
4. **Test at night hours** (set system clock or wait) to see reduced roaming distances

> [!TIP]
> If you have a way to fast-forward server ticks or override the time check, that would make testing time-of-day behavior much faster. Otherwise you can temporarily hardcode `isNightTime()` to return `true` for testing.
